  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1219 AM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe start of next week has present model agreement seeing the\ncurrent upper-level high retrograde back west during the course of\nthe week. This retrograde will eventually see said high back over\nthe Panhandles resulting in a return of the more widespread\ntriple-digit temperatures. This will also see chances of\nprecipitation start to decrease with chances Monday only around 10\nto 30 percent and Tuesday now dropping below 10 percent. However,\npresent GFS runs have continue to hint at the possibility of a new\ntrough digging south into the area later in the week that could\nprove to provide us with cooler temperatures and better chances at\nprecipitation. Present ensembles have also picked up on the idea\nwith current NBM now giving us a 10 to 20 percent chance of seeing\nprecipitation starting Wednesday. However, given that this trough\nhas been very inconsistent between the different runs, confidence\nis not too high on the idea just yet.",
